       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day for extended-release.\n- A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum per dose of about 1,000 mg. Doses this high raise the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis.\n\nWas this a typo? Some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.**\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, divided into doses. For example, 850 mg PO twice daily.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and give a clinical rationale. I'd still advise checking with pharmacy first."
      }
